{
  "$schema": "https://kinetixui.com/schema/icon-mapping.json",
  "description": "Cross-platform mapping for icons KinetixUI COMPONENTS render internally (their own expand chevron, checkmark, close button, etc.) — not icons a caller passes in as a prop/children, which stay free-form per platform by design and are out of scope here. lucide-react remains the single React icon source; native ports each use their own platform-native icon mechanism (Material Icons on Flutter, SF Symbols on SwiftUI) or, on Jetpack Compose, plain Unicode glyphs — Compose uses ZERO `Icons.*` (Material Icons) references anywhere in this codebase today, confirmed by exhaustive grep across every port file. This file only covers icon names reused across two or more components; single-component icons (e.g. Rating's Star, ColorPicker's Pipette) aren't covered by this slice — see /docs/icons for the full list of what's not yet mapped.",
  "types": {
    "icon-ref": "a named icon reference from the platform's own built-in icon set (Flutter Icons.*, SwiftUI SF Symbol systemName)",
    "glyph": "a literal Unicode character rendered as plain text (e.g. Compose's Text(text = \"▾\")), not a named icon asset",
    "shape": "a custom-drawn shape (Circle(), CircleShape, BoxShape.circle, Canvas), not an icon or a text glyph",
    "absent": "no hardcoded icon-like element found in this platform's port of this component — verified by grep, not assumed. Usually means the platform's own built-in widget draws its own affordance (e.g. a native context-menu's checkmark), or the element genuinely isn't rendered on that platform."
  },
